<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: AIB says Sutherland resigns from board.</title>
<headline>AIB says Sutherland resigns from board.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allied Irish Banks Plc said on Tuesday that it had accepted with regret the resignation of Peter Sutherland as a non-executive director.  </p>
<p>Sutherland, who will resign with immediate effect, has served on the AIB board for six years. He was chairman from 1989 to 1993, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;His decision to resign at this juncture follows his recent appointment as chairman of the British Petroleum Company Plc when it was intimated he would be reviewing his heavy business commitments,&quot; AIB said.</p>
<p>Sutherland is also chairman and managing director of Goldman Sachs International.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
